<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 123 0 R/Pg 29 0 R/A[1188 0 R 0]/K[81]>>
endobj
686 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 124 0 R/E(How many candidates do you think will apply?)/Pg 30 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj
687 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 124 0 R/E(Traditionally you can expect around 5-12 interim superintendent candidates. The location, hiring timeline, and benefits package, among other factors will contribute to the total number of applicants.  )/Pg 30 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj
688 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 124 0 R/E(Will the board see all candidates that apply?)/Pg 30 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj
689 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 124 0 R/E(Yes. Candidate materials \(cover letter, resume, and references\) are shared with the board each week.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj
690 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 124 0 R/E<5768656E206172652063616E6469646174657390206E616D6573206D616465207075626C69633F>/Pg 30 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj
691 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 124 0 R/E(Candidates' applications are confidential until they would be named as finalists for the position. Normally, there would not be more than two to three finalists made public.  The board will decide when/if finalists names are shared publicly.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj
692 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 124 0 R/E(What if a candidate is not brought to the board as a finalist who a board member thinks should be?)/Pg 30 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj
693 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 124 0 R/E(GLS will present EVERY candidate to the board; an objective rating \(based on the desired qualifications identified earlier in the process\) will be made by the firm and shared with the board. However, the board will select semifinalists and finalists. We do the behind-the-scenes work, but it is the board's responsibility to make these decisions.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj
694 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 124 0 R/E(What if the board does not agree on a candidate after the formal interviews?)/Pg 30 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj
695 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 124 0 R/E<>/Pg 30 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj
